# Authors: Simon Davidson & Claude | Created 2026-08-19 | Last modified 2026-08-19
#
# tb_config_manager with CFG_MEM_SYNC=1 and WORDS_PER_CONFIG=16 — the opt-in
# fully-pipelined config engine, paired with a 1-cycle REGISTERED cfg memory
# model (which is what every real build actually instantiates: shared/bram_sdp.v
# on FPGA, a deployment SRAM model on the ASIC).
#
# Expects 19 cycles of config push, versus 34 in the default latency-agnostic
# mode and 49 before either. Also covers the holding buffer under both memory
# back-pressure (T5) and accelerator back-pressure (T6), which is where a
# pipelined reader would otherwise drop the word already in flight.
xrun -sv -timescale 10ps/1ps -access wrc -top tb_config_manager \
  -define CFG_SYNC -define WPC16 \
  config_manager.v tb_config_manager.v
